{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A psalm. Sing to YHWH a new song</b> — for He has saved him with His right hand, like: \"and my arm saved me\" [Genesis 32:11; לי זרועי read as זרועו, \"his arm\"]." "And the meaning of <b>and His holy arm</b> — is that it is outstretched and reaches the place of His desire. Perhaps this psalm concerns the coming of the redeemer."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 98, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:32.386187619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}